# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Authority material is large and content-addressed. The registry
# (forensics/authorities/AUTHORITIES.json) IS checked in, because it is the
# evidence that binds claims to hashes. The per-file SOURCE_MANIFEST.*.json is
# also checked in: it is tamper-evidence for the extracted source tree, so that
# the recorded root hash is verifiable without re-downloading. Only the
# archives, extracted trees, build directories and installed prefixes are
# reproducible-and-ignored.
/forensics/authorities/downloads/
/forensics/authorities/src/
/forensics/authorities/build/
/forensics/authorities/prefix/
/forensics/authorities/captures/

# Court scratch material produced inside the container.
/court/

# Phase 2 distribution shell: the bulky artifacts are generated and reproducible
# from forensics/tools/build_phase2.sh (the version scripts, pkg-config metadata,
# shell manifest and court results ARE committed as evidence).
/artifacts/phase2/*.so
/artifacts/phase2/*.so.*
/artifacts/phase2/*.a
/artifacts/phase2/include/
/artifacts/phase2/shell/

# Gemel's local evidence-native working store. It is ~95 MB (it snapshots the
# derived atlas) and is a local working memory, not a deliverable: it is
# recreated with `gemel init` + the recorded change/checkpoint in
# forensics/STATUS.md and docs/DECISIONS.md. FRF's store IS committed (below),
# because its receipts and claims are the claim-bearing evidence.
/.gemel/

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
.DS_Store
